  "verification": [
    "Independent number-state sums and matrices check amplitudes, probabilities, separately weighted tails, microscopic reverse transitions and finite-boundary commutators against the fixed references and the existing Python API.",
    "Course integration preserves disclosures, unfinished responses, notes and original calculator drafts; explicit copying preserves the exact chosen temperature and waits for manual calculation.",
    "Strict source metadata preserves file/text hash identity, tolerances, basis/origin and wavevector transforms and single/double-valued selection through workbench export and explicitly saved research records. Changed requests cannot inherit unrelated source metadata.",
    "Official Cu source bytes, lossless XZ decompression, input-cell normalization and all thermal rows are checked. Import loading, replacement, cancellation and stale completion are exercised through actual form handlers."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "Fixed teaching references do not introduce a general oscillator or scattering solver. Holstein vacuum and numerical truncation panels do not infer a finite-temperature polaron state.",
    "A source checksum identifies the parsed source; it is not an electronic-structure calculation or magnetic-order detector. Imported metadata cannot independently reverify absent original bytes. Numerical representation validity and standard-label coverage remain separate.",
    "Cu thermal_properties data describe one official calculated four-atom input cell at one volume. They do not supply eigenvectors, measured data, full quasi-harmonic volume predictions or a newly performed material calculation.",
    "This release covers three learning hooks and representative source workflows. Broader curriculum depth, diagnosis and authentic workflows for every tool family remain open."
  ],
